{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — Cart icon and count
  Phase 8. The inside of the header's cart control.

  Two consumers, which is why it is a snippet: sections/header.liquid renders
  it inline, and sections/cart-icon-bubble.liquid renders it alone as the
  target the cart script swaps in after every cart change. Dawn keeps two
  copies of this markup in parallel and they drift; one snippet cannot.

  Usage:
  {% render 'cart-icon-bubble' %}

  THE COUNT IS cart.item_count, NEVER A LITERAL.
  Phase 1 NAV-09 recorded the prototype's badge as the character 0, painted on
  whether or not anything was in a cart that did not exist. An empty cart shows
  no badge at all here, so nothing announces "0 items" — the control's own name
  is still "Cart", which is the whole message when the cart is empty.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% render 'icon-cart' %}
<span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'header.cart' | t }}</span>
{%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
  <span class="header__cart-count" data-cart-count aria-hidden="true">
    {{- cart.item_count -}}
  </span>
  <span class="visually-hidden" data-cart-count-text>
    {{- 'cart.item_count' | t: count: cart.item_count -}}
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
